PRIOR WORK
----------

PorterPacker started life as an addon written by Ivaar, later modified by
Gimlic and Siyual. Working out how to talk to the Porter Moogle at all -- which
packets carry the menu, where the slip index sits, how the contents bitfield is
laid out, which sentinel closes the dialog -- was their doing, and it is the
hard part of this addon.

The code here is not theirs. Every module was written for this project: the
packet layer, the inventory primitives, the trade orchestration, the per
character data format and the messaging. What carries over from the original is
the protocol knowledge itself -- packet identifiers, byte offsets, zone and menu
ids -- which is factual description of how the game behaves rather than
authored expression.

Credit for that discovery belongs to Ivaar, Gimlic and Siyual, and this notice
exists to record it.

The original is published without a license at:

    https://github.com/Ivaar/Windower-addons

Anyone with a claim to that work who sees it differently is welcome to raise it:

    https://github.com/ejouanchicot/PorterPacker/issues
